course: dictionary
lesson: 11497
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Agitate is a verb with three main meanings: to make someone worried or upset, to shake or stir a liquid hard, and to campaign publicly for a change.
explain: «The loud thunder agitated the puppy, and it hid under the bed.» The puppy was frightened and upset, so agitated means to make someone worried or upset.
explain: «Agitate the jar of sand and water well.» Here there is no worry at all. The jar is being shaken hard, so agitate means to shake or stir. A washing machine works the same way when it agitates the clothes.
explain: «The villagers agitated for a new school.» People cannot agitate a school, so the clue is for. Here agitate means to campaign, to argue loudly and publicly until the change happens.
fact: Agitate is a verb: agitate, agitates, agitated, agitating.
fact: «Agitate» can mean to make someone worried, nervous or upset.
fact: «Agitate» can mean to shake or stir a liquid hard.
fact: «Agitate for» or «agitate against» means to campaign publicly for or against a change.
fact: To find the meaning, look at the clues: a frightened person, a shaking liquid, or a group arguing for change.
exercise: «The barking dog agitated the nervous baby.» What does agitated mean here? | Happy and full of song | Calm and sleepy | *Worried and upset | Shiny and clean
exercise: «Shake the jar to agitate the sand and water.» What does agitate mean in this sentence? | *Shake or stir the liquid hard | Freeze the water | Paint the jar | Pour the water away slowly
exercise: «The students agitated for a new library.» What does agitated for mean? | *Campaigned publicly for a change | Forgot where the library was | Read books quietly alone | Slept in the library
test:
«The news agitated the crowd, and people began to shout.» What does agitated mean here? | Calmly asleep | *Worried, nervous or upset | Very sweet to taste | Quietly reading
test:
«Agitate the paint well before you start to paint.» What does agitate mean in this sentence? | Ignore the paint | Wash the brushes | *Shake or stir hard | Throw the paint away
exam:
«Pupils agitated against the new rule, and the school changed it.» What does agitated against mean? | Ate their lunch quietly | *Campaigned publicly to make a change happen | Fell fast asleep | Wrote the rule down
